WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.615 --> 00:00:02.490
RETO MEIER: Today we're
talking about Pub/Sub

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:06.030
in Cloud Monitoring and an
AI-searchable Video Archive.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.340
I'm Reto Meier, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.200
where we serve you
the lowest latency

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.110
news from the safety of home.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.610
Cloud Monitoring
is a service that

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.760
can alert you through a variety
of notification channels, which

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.100
now includes Cloud Pub/Sub.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.140
Pub/Sub is a
publish/subscribe queue

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.230
that lets you build loosely
coupled applications.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.360
With this integration,
currently in beta,

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.880
you can create automated
and programmatic workflows

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.930
in response to alerts.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.700
For example, by integrating
with third party providers

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.420
to create an incident
response workflow.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.780
We've just published the first
episode of Google Cloud Drawing

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.960
Board, a new video series that
breaks down various Google

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.850
Cloud tools and shows you how
they work and what they can do.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.690
In the first video,
Priyanka Vergadia

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.510
covers Compute Engine,
showing off various use cases

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.340
and how you can use
it for your projects

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.710
while managing your costs.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.620
Last week, Dale
Markowitz shared a post

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.680
explaining how she used Google
Cloud to build an AI-searchable

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.260
Video Archive as a
Father's Day gift.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.710
She took over 456 hours
of digitized footage

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.870
in Google Drive and
created a way for her dad

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.360
to rediscover forgotten moments.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.780
And then she turned around
and showed us how she did it.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.910
It's a pretty fantastic
read, and it demonstrates

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.670
that while building a searchable
index for video archive

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.160
is fun for personal
projects, it's

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.780
also useful for
businesses looking

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.610
to automatically generate
metadata for large video data

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.570
sets, caption and translate
clips, or quickly search

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.940
brand and creative assets.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.730
We're only three weeks away
from Google Cloud Next.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.550
For 2020, we've reimagined
this annual conference

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.430
into a 9-week digital event.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.220
There's a lot to explore, so
we've created session packages

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.530
to help attendees discover
and explore sessions

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:47.700
that they're interested in.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.200
Check these out for
yourself, and be

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.910
sure to add a package
to your playlist

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.327
so that you don't miss a thing.

00:01:53.327 --> 00:01:55.410
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.910
or see the full list,
check out the link.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:01.000
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.590
We'll see you in the cloud.

